# Batch files MUST be checked out with CRLF, on every platform and regardless of
# the user's core.autocrlf setting.
#
# cmd.exe tracks its position in a running .bat by byte offset. With LF-only
# line endings it mis-seeks after returning from `call :label` and silently
# skips the following line - no error, no output, the statement simply never
# runs. It cost a debugging session here: the installer copied one file, skipped
# the next, and the uninstaller then could not find its helper.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# PowerShell is not affected the same way, but keeping it CRLF avoids surprises
# in editors and in the release ZIP.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Everything else: normalise in the repository, check out per platform.
* text=auto

# Binary assets must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.lib binary
*.zip binary
